# Golden Pathway CRM conventions

This CRM was imported from an internal baseline and then stripped. The removals
below are deliberate; do not reintroduce them.

## Removed on purpose — do not add back

- **No physical mail.** There is no packet manager, no FedEx, no print vendor,
  no shipping, no tracking numbers, and no `delivery_method`. Welcome packets are
  delivered by e-signature only.
- **No third department.** Staff departments are exactly two:
  `profiles.is_accounts` (Account Managers) and `profiles.is_services`
  (Client Services). There is no compliance department, no
  `assigned_compliance_id`, and no `compliance_verification` stage.
- **No Sentry, RingCentral, Trigger.dev, ElevenLabs, Tenor, DocuSign, OpenSign,
  or Shape CRM importer.** If error tracking or telephony is wanted later, it is
  a fresh decision, not a restoration.

## Roles vs. departments

They are different axes and both must be checked.

- **Role** (`profiles.role`, enum `user_role`): `dev`, `admin`, `acct_manager`,
  `attorney`, `client`. Capability predicates live in `lib/roles.ts` — add one
  there instead of inlining a role comparison.
- **Department** (booleans on `profiles`): `is_accounts`, `is_services`. A person
  may be in both. Filter assignee dropdowns through
  `lib/team/department-members.ts`.

Any role or permission change must be made in all three layers together:
`middleware.ts` route gates, the `lib/roles.ts` predicate, and the Postgres RLS
policy. Row Level Security is the security boundary — never client-side
filtering.

## MIDs

A MID is a **label**, never a tenancy or visibility boundary. Every staff member
sees every client regardless of MID; do not add MID-scoped RLS.

- `mids` is the source of truth. There is no hardcoded merchant list.
- `clients.mid_id` is chosen at creation and follows the client through to
  attorney hand-off. Read it by join; never re-infer it.
- Financial and legal records snapshot the MID *name* at the time they are
  produced (`esign_requests`, `refunds`), so renaming a MID cannot rewrite
  history.

## E-Sign

Adding a MID and its documents must stay **fully no-code**: an admin enters a MID
name, uploads PDFs, and places fields with the drag-and-drop editor. Never
reintroduce a hardcoded document-kind union, a per-kind `switch`, a per-kind
`CHECK` constraint, or a PDF bundled into the repo. See
`.cursor/rules/esign-and-uploads.mdc`.

## Before changing shared code

Shared surfaces — sidebars, role checks, `client_notes`, email sequence tables,
MID pickers, e-sign templates, the Attorney Queue and public batch downloads,
onboarding stage gates — are used from many places. Grep for every call site
before editing, and run `pnpm tsc --noEmit`.
